// CHECKPOINTS run by each language community.
//
// FLANDERS (huisonderwijs, declared to AGODI — per the official
// Flanders.be guidance): register with the Examencommissie
// Basisonderwijs by the school year the child turns 11; hold the
// basic-education certificate by the year they turn 13; register with
// the Examencommissie secundair by 15; hold the first-cycle secondary
// certificate by 16. Late registration or failure at the required age
// means compulsory school enrolment. Parents bear all costs.
//
// WALLONIA-BRUSSELS / FWB (enseignement a domicile, annual
// declaration): CEB (end of primary), CE1D, and CE2D checkpoints via
// the community's certification exams and jury routes. TWO VERIFIED
