// a requirement for a detailed pedagogical project and a yearly
// training plan with closer follow-up, and pass thresholds for
// CEB/CE1D/CESS rise to 60% from the June 2027 examinations.
// Brussels families choose which community to declare to.
//
// THE CORE HONESTY POINT — DO NOT SOFTEN: an online or foreign school
// that is not officially recognised by the family's community is
// legally treated as HOME EDUCATION in Belgium. Enrolment with
// Smartious therefore does NOT exempt a family from the declaration
// or the checkpoint exams — the two tracks run together, and every
// page says so plainly. This is the Belgian equivalent of the
// Spain/Portugal honesty discipline.
//
// After the age-16 first-cycle checkpoint in Flanders, the mandated
